<title>ALBANIA: Albania reopens railway link to Montenegro.</title>
<headline>Albania reopens railway link to Montenegro.</headline>
<dateline>TIRANA 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Albania opened its railway link with neighbouring Montenegro on Monday after a four-year break, the Albanian news Agency ATA reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The line, closed in 1992 after the United Nations imposed a trade embargo on rump Yugoslavia, links Bajze, 140 km north of Tirana, with Tuz in Montenegro.</p>
